  "id": "DrugBank_DB12874 - MONDO_grouped_18874_4643",
  "verbalization": "Quizartinib is associated with Myeloid Leukemia through a series of indications that collectively suggest a potential role in the treatment of this condition. The drug is indicated for Acute Myeloid Leukemia with specific genetic mutations, such as Npm1 somatic mutations, T(9;11)(p22;q23), and those associated with Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation. These conditions are all classified under the broader category of Myeloid Leukemia, indicating a shared pathophysiological context. The presence of Tioguanine as an indication for these leukemias further suggests a possible pathway involving chemotherapy agents, which may be used in combination with Quizartinib. The integration of these indications implies that Quizartinib may be part of a broader therapeutic strategy for Myeloid Leukemia, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
